  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "17862064",
      "title": "A Closer Look at \"ng new\"",
      "lectureOrder": 735,
      "videoOrder": 675,
      "sourceHash": "530a43bf5c9f4fb0a2fa1badec88652f053d98d64213370b5711dbb1f2d76c44",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.62,
          "en": "Instructor: And to dive in, let's create a new project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.62,
          "end": 6.9,
          "en": "Now for that, make sure you are using the latest version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.9,
          "end": 11.9,
          "en": "of the CLI with \"npm install -g @angular/cli@latest.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.36,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "On Mac and Linux, you might need to add a pseudo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 17.73,
          "en": "in front of this, on Windows you don't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.73,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "Now, once you got that installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 22.17,
          "en": "once you got that latest version installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.17,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "let's create a brand new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 26.97,
          "en": "and you know how that works, with \"ng new.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.97,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "Now actually, before we create such a project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.84,
          "en": "let's hit enter here, without entering any name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.84,
          "end": 36.18,
          "en": "Now what you'll see is that if you do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "you actually all are prompted for a project name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "So you can also use the command in this shorter way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "Now let me skip this or cancel this with Ctrl+C for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "and type \"ng new --help.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 53.61,
          "en": "The \"--help\" flag can be used after any command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.61,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "to learn more about the command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 58.38,
          "en": "and the different configuration options you have available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.38,
          "end": 61.71,
          "en": "So in this case, if I hit enter, you see there are a bunch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.71,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "of flags we could add after the command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 68.49,
          "en": "So we could type ng new, some name of our choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.49,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "and then for example, \"--collection,\" or \"--commit.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "And here you see a description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 76.95,
          "en": "of what these configuration flags do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.95,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "Now these flags change over time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "new options are added, some options are deprecated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 85.26,
          "en": "So going through all of them doesn't make a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.26,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "of sense here, but there are some which I wanna draw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "your attention to. This here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 94.44,
          "en": "will it become important later, create application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.44,
          "end": 98.31,
          "en": "It's set to true by default, so you only need to add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.31,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "if you want to disable this, and right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 104.16,
          "en": "this doesn't make much sense to us, but we'll later see why",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.16,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "this command can become very important and useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "It can become important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "if you wanna manage multiple applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 115.8,
          "en": "and libraries inside of one Angular CLI managed project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.8,
          "end": 118.203,
          "en": "again, more on that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.19,
          "end": 123.42,
          "en": "Dry run can also be interesting if you just want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.42,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "to see what these CLI would do with your command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 130.83,
          "en": "with the ng new command here without actually creating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.83,
          "end": 132.54,
          "en": "the content on the disc.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "This might sound like it doesn't make much sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "but if you're passing multiple configuration flags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 142.47,
          "en": "adding \"--dry-run\" will spit out what",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.47,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "the CLI will do thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "so that you can verify whether you will get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "the project you want without actually going",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.34,
          "en": "through the full setup process and writing everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.34,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "to the disc, which can be nice at times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "With inline style and inline template, you can set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 161.79,
          "en": "whether new components you're going to generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.79,
          "end": 164.1,
          "en": "will actually start with inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.1,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "or inline templates or with external files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "This can save you the hassle of setting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 172.803,
          "en": "for every newly generated component individually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.45,
          "end": 177.75,
          "en": "The prefix command allows you to configure the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.75,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "prefix every new component you generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 182.58,
          "en": "with the ng generate command will have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.58,
          "end": 184.59,
          "en": "Now let me also note at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.59,
          "end": 188.13,
          "en": "that many or most of these options actually can be changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.13,
          "end": 190.44,
          "en": "to the existing project later too.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.44,
          "end": 192.39,
          "en": "And I will show you where to change them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 194.82,
          "en": "and where to generally adjust the configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.82,
          "end": 196.503,
          "en": "in a separate lecture, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 200.1,
          "en": "Routing allows you to specify whether you wanna start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.1,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "with a routing module and some initial routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 204.75,
          "en": "Skip tests allows you to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.75,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "whether newly generated components and services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 210.51,
          "en": "and so on, will have testing files next to them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.51,
          "end": 213.39,
          "en": "Skip install allows you to create a new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 215.46,
          "en": "with the files written to the disc,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.46,
          "end": 218.43,
          "en": "without the npm dependencies being installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.43,
          "end": 221.34,
          "en": "This speeds up the creation process and you can then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.34,
          "end": 224.94,
          "en": "always install the dependencies manually later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.94,
          "end": 227.07,
          "en": "So these are some interesting options here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.07,
          "end": 231.78,
          "en": "and \"ng new --help\" allows you to go through them in detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.78,
          "end": 234.84,
          "en": "In addition, always check out the official documentation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.84,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "and that is true for all the things that we'll be showing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 239.67000000000002,
          "en": "throughout this module, I will also reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 239.67000000000002,
          "end": 241.95,
          "en": "the official docs from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.95,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "There you find the latest up to date information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 248.52,
          "en": "about Angular, the CLI, the different configuration files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 248.52,
          "end": 251.1,
          "en": "it uses and for example here for the CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.1,
          "end": 254.31,
          "en": "you find a list of all the commands it supports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.31,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "the aliases, so the shortcuts you could use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "and of course then if you click on a command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 261.72,
          "en": "you find detailed information about this command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 261.72,
          "end": 264.69,
          "en": "what it does and which options you can set there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 264.69,
          "end": 266.46,
          "en": "You see a bit more information about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 266.46,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "the different configuration options here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "So definitely all to check out these pages here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "if you wanna learn more about the CLI in general",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 276.03,
          "en": "or the individual commands.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.03,
          "end": 279.21,
          "en": "With that, let's create a new project here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 279.21,
          "end": 283.86,
          "en": "So here I'm going to write \"ng new angular-config\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 283.86,
          "end": 286.8,
          "en": "and simply hit enter without any additional flags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.8,
          "end": 288.9,
          "en": "Now then here I get asked whether I want to add routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.9,
          "end": 290.61,
          "en": "and I'll choose \"N\" for no here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 290.61,
          "end": 294.65999999999997,
          "en": "and I'll choose CSS as my well, style sheet format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.65999999999997,
          "end": 298.02,
          "en": "so that I don't wanna use SaaS or SCCS here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.02,
          "end": 300.39,
          "en": "which you could do though. You can choose that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 300.39,
          "end": 301.83,
          "en": "and then you can write your styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 301.83,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "with a style pre-processor, like SaaS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 307.62,
          "en": "Now since I didn't choose dry run, or skip install,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 307.62,
          "end": 310.95,
          "en": "this creates the full project, installs all dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 310.95,
          "end": 314.28,
          "en": "and writes everything to the disc, and I'll be back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 314.28,
          "end": 316.443,
          "en": "in a new lecture once this is finished.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
